# Architecture

This repository is a Next.js application starter. App-Framework owns reusable packages, shared Cursor standards, the reusable static deploy workflow, and the capability catalogue. Do not reimplement those here.

- Application routes, styling, and configuration values stay in this repository.
- Import `@app-framework/app-config` and `@app-framework/dev-tools` from the package root only. Do not add `@app-framework/ui` until a registry release exists.
- Use published semver ranges. Do not add a `file:` or `git` dependency on App-Framework.
- Shared coding rules are the pinned copy in `.cursor/rules/framework/`. Do not edit that copy in place. Product rules belong in the generated application's own `.cursor/rules`.
- Propose a new shared capability in App-Framework instead of copying it into the template.
- Do not add optional product features, a component library, or a second catalogue without a real requirement.
- `pnpm check` is the full verification. Pre-commit stays limited to lint-staged.
- Keep the current deploy workflow until the tag `deploy-static-v1` exists. Do not point this repository at that tag before then.

The ownership split is documented in `docs/RESPONSIBILITIES.md`.
